TITLE:: Pvomm
SUMMARY:: Experimental PPM-C variable-order generation
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/PgraphWalk, Classes/Pseed, Guides/Patternarium-Systems

DESCRIPTION::
Experimental: this API may change before 1.0.

Trains suffix-context counts independently for each stream. Generation begins at the longest available suffix of the start context and backs off through shorter contexts. At an eligible context, PPM-C gives each symbol count/(totalCount+typeCount), with escape probability typeCount/(totalCount+typeCount). ExcludeSeen removes already considered symbols from lower-order counts.

This generator uses the closed observed alphabet: no unobserved symbols are invented. If an eligible context covers every remaining symbol, escape is suppressed and its counts are normalized directly, since escape would have no destination. This finite-alphabet boundary rule is distinct from compressing an unknown byte alphabet. Escapes remain possible even from a context with only one observed continuation when other symbols remain.

A corpus whose elements are all SequenceableCollections is interpreted as separate sequences. Otherwise it is one sequence. Empty subsequences are permitted, but at least one symbol is required. Contexts never cross training sequence boundaries. Array-valued symbols can be represented inside an explicitly nested single-sequence corpus. Nil symbols are invalid. Symbol objects retain identity; use stable, immutable objects as context keys.

Learning updates only the current stream's model after selecting each symbol. Its tables can grow substantially over a long stream; no global trained model is shared. MaxOrder is at most 64 and training accepts at most 1000000 symbols. Training stores suffix keys and counts; key-copy work can be O(corpus length times maxOrder squared). Sampling scans the observed alphabet for each available order. Learning memory depends on the distinct observed contexts. Output indices have an explicit machine-Integer guard. Seed and numerical calculations use sclang's thread RNG and Pseed.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: corpus
Literal nonempty SequenceableCollection or collection of separate sequences; no model is shared between streams.
ARGUMENT:: maxOrder
Nonnegative Integer, default 8, at most 64; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: start
Nil, a symbol, or a context collection; a Function is evaluated once with inval. The context is truncated to maxOrder.
ARGUMENT:: learning
Boolean, default false; sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: excludeSeen
Boolean, default true; sampled once. Once-sampled flags/counts accept literals, Functions or Patterns.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments in public constructor order.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval when the stream ends.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Pvomm([0, 2, 0, 4, 0, 2], length: 16)).asStream.all;
::

Node or symbol identities become pitches/chords, exposing repeated paths and context choices. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pvomm / Value stream
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Pvomm([0, 2, 0, 4, 0, 2], length: 16)).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { tones[x[\node]] ? 0 } { if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 } }, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical example
Load the main Guide example instruments first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano,
    \degree, Pseed(Pseq([42]), Pvomm([0, 2, 4, 2, 0, 7, 4, 2], 3, 32)),
    \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Informative long contexts
code::
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Pvomm([\a, \b, \x, \a, \c, \y, \a, \b, \x], 2, 16, [\a, \b])).asStream.all;
::

Node or symbol identities become pitches/chords, exposing repeated paths and context choices. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pvomm / Informative long contexts
var values = {
Pseed(Pseq([42]), Pvomm([\a, \b, \x, \a, \c, \y, \a, \b, \x], 2, 16, [\a, \b])).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isKindOf(Dictionary)) { tones[x[\node]] ? 0 } { if(x.isNumber) { x } { tones[x] ? 0 } }, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

